From 3c06a8e80be575aaf966d735776dea1a237d4ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:04:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(settings): add file_exists_action setting
 (rename/overwrite)

Surge always auto-renamed a download whose destination file already
existed. Add a General setting, file_exists_action, that keeps rename as
the default and adds overwrite, which reuses the existing name so the
completed download replaces the old file.

Overwrite never targets a name owned by an active download, a pending
.surge working file or a directory; those still fall back to name(N).ext.
finalizeCompletedFile now only treats an existing final path as success
when the working file is gone, so a failed replace is reported instead
of silently keeping the old file.

The TUI cycles the value with Enter (shown as < Rename > / < Overwrite >),
and docs/SETTINGS.md documents the new key.

Refs #265
